session, what we'll do

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.503
is we'll talk through
a little bit about how

00:00:10.503 --> 00:00:15.240
we think about security
at Google and in G Suite.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.000
And then we will show
you some of the products

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.040
that we have that can
remove some of that work

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.360
that you're having to do.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.703
And then we will spend
some time in demos.

00:00:24.703 --> 00:00:26.370
We'll spend quite a
bit of time in demos

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.700
because we think it's helpful
to see how these things work.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.410
And then we'll
finish up by having

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.560
one of our partners, Sumo Logic,
talk about their experience

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.800
in integrating through our
APIs, and how they are helping

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.850
you automate what
you're doing as well.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:46.160
So with that, security is
increasingly difficult.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.970
There are more and more
attacks, and those attacks

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.380
are more and more sophisticated.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:56.050
So, as administrators
and security staff,

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.380
it is something that is
increasingly difficult

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:02.840
to protect your users'
devices and data.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.190
So at G Suite, what
we try to do is

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:08.860
we try to think through how
we can provide you the tools

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.460
that you need to really cover
the different threats that

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.480
are coming at you, and ensure
that you are best protected

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.770
against those.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.100
We've had the chance to
have a lot of conversations

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.830
with our customers, partners,
and analysts, and what we see

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.990
is reoccurring themes.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.510
There's a lot of
security tools out there

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.450
that give you a lot of
data, but at the same time,

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:39.040
they fail to provide really
actionable, valuable insights.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.740
Those that do provide
good insights, many times,

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.170
lack the controls
and tools that you

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.240
need to go in and
remediate those things

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.220
and fix them quickly.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.090
And the solutions that do manage
to provide both of those to you

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:54.860
are, many times, very complex.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:58.660
They require specific expertise
that are very hard to find,

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.450
or a lot of training that
takes a lot of time and energy

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.980
and money.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.650
So what we see is we see
a lot of organizations

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:10.660
that have security tools that
are partially implemented,

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.540
and they're planning on
continuing to implement

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.010
those and finish them.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.230
Or they finish the
implementation,

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.810
but they're just not sure
how to effectively leverage

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.190
those tools.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:27.580
So the guiding principle
that we are using at G Suite

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.440
is, how can we provide
you a comprehensive set

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.680
of tools that is, at the same
time, simple and easy to use?

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.940
And so we want to
cover all of your needs

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:43.060
and all of the various threats
that are coming at you,

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:44.770
but at the same
time, we want you

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:47.020
to be able to pick up those
tools and start using them

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.240
and start finding value.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.640
And so, over the
last year, you've

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.510
seen a lot of launches
coming in security,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.020
and these are just
a few of those.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:04.120
Things like automatic enrollment
in Google management--

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.390
Google device management.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.310
So when a user
comes in with a BYOD

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.490
and they sign in with their
corporate credentials,

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:15.370
it's automatically enrolled
for light management.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:18.970
And that allows you to see
what data those devices

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.960
are accessing and exactly
what those devices are doing,

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.330
and it also allows you
to wipe corporate data

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.270
from those devices.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.540
Security health and the
security dashboards,

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.030
which give you a high-level
overview of important security

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.070
metrics from your organization.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:39.490
The Investigation tool, which
allows you to dive in quickly,

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:43.150
get deep in the data, and
take remediative steps.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.880
The Alert Center, where we
communicate the most important

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:49.600
things to you that you should
look into, and proactively

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.860
let you know about things
that are happening.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.320
And then, of course, Gmail.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.250
And Gmail, we know, is a
huge vector of attack--

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.390
email, in general, I should say.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:00.640
So we are constantly
investing in Gmail

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:06.550
to ensure that it is very secure
and covering all of your needs,

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.260
and making sure that
your users are protected.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.310
We've launched things like
Security Sandbox, Confidential

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:18.019
Mode, and business email
compromise protections.

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:20.950
And so we're consistently adding
more and more tools for you

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:27.170
there so that Gmail is the
best possible solution for you.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:32.020
However, as we continue to talk
to our customers, one thing

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.790
we consistently hear--

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.370
and I'm sure you guys
have heard this as well--

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.750
is that there's
always too much to do.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:43.840
There's always that one product,
or that one vector of attack

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.080
that you're trying to get to
that you just can't because you

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.390
