00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.950
And so first, Data
Loss Prevention.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.990
If you're not familiar
with the product,

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.520
basically what it
is is the ability

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:49.000
to create rules
in Gmail and Drive

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.810
to detect certain
patterns, whether that's

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:59.200
strings or regex, or using one
of the predefined detectors

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:03.370
to block exfiltration
before it happens,

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:07.480
or also to detect malicious
information before it

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:09.527
comes into your organization.

00:10:09.527 --> 00:10:11.860
One of the really cool things
about Data Loss Prevention

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.550
is it's built right
into the product,

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.400
so it stops things
before they happen.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.940
So it's not something
that happens,

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:21.100
and then DLP goes
in and cleans it up.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.560
It actually prevents
documents from being

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.510
shared in the first place.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:28.010
We'll show you a little bit
more about what that looks like.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:31.690
But for the updates for
DLP, what we've done

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:35.020
is we've unified the experience
of creating these rules,

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:36.820
but then also, we've
really invested

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:40.160
in logging and visibility around
what these rules are doing.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.370
We've gotten a lot
