00:30:59.750 --> 00:31:02.550
So there might be something
going on with this user.

00:31:02.550 --> 00:31:04.100
We can dig in
deeper and actually

00:31:04.100 --> 00:31:05.370
figure out what's happening.

00:31:05.370 --> 00:31:09.030
So we can dig in and
remediate this specific issue.

00:31:09.030 --> 00:31:14.910
So we'll pivot on this user, and
we'll look at Gmail log events

00:31:14.910 --> 00:31:17.880
where this user
received the email.

00:31:17.880 --> 00:31:20.220
And we'll say,
specifically, we want

00:31:20.220 --> 00:31:26.130
to see emails that are not
from our current organization.

00:31:26.130 --> 00:31:29.110
So we'll copy that.

00:31:29.110 --> 00:31:31.750
And also, we want
to filter out emails

00:31:31.750 --> 00:31:35.950
that are from Google and
that we don't want to see

00:31:35.950 --> 00:31:38.760
the alerts that are coming in.

00:31:38.760 --> 00:31:41.960
And then when we query for
that, what this will show

00:31:41.960 --> 00:31:44.900
us is the external emails
that this user received.

00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:47.570
So we want to see potentially
how this user was compromised

00:31:47.570 --> 00:31:49.310
by a phishing email.

00:31:49.310 --> 00:31:54.690
So we see several different
emails that came in.

00:31:54.690 --> 00:31:59.390
Specifically, we can look at the
log events for what happened.

00:31:59.390 --> 00:32:03.650
It looks like this user
only opened and clicked

00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:04.880
