00:41:00.580 --> 00:41:03.540
and data from Alert Center.

00:41:03.540 --> 00:41:05.760
So let's take a look
at an example of how

00:41:05.760 --> 00:41:07.800
Sumo Logic can help
monitor, detect,

00:41:07.800 --> 00:41:10.570
and investigate threats.

00:41:10.570 --> 00:41:13.440
So this is our G Suite
overview dashboard

00:41:13.440 --> 00:41:16.320
that shows a summary of
all the activity that's

00:41:16.320 --> 00:41:17.820
happening in G Suite.

00:41:17.820 --> 00:41:22.710
And we have drilldowns
specific to Alert Center.

00:41:22.710 --> 00:41:25.770
This shows Alert Center
Overview dashboard

00:41:25.770 --> 00:41:29.130
that shows all the data that
we've gotten from Alert Center

00:41:29.130 --> 00:41:30.810
so far.

00:41:30.810 --> 00:41:33.620
So here, we see an example
of a user's credentials

00:41:33.620 --> 00:41:34.838
being compromised.

00:41:34.838 --> 00:41:37.130
And I just want to point out
the level of detail that's

00:41:37.130 --> 00:41:38.660
coming in from
Alert Center, where

00:41:38.660 --> 00:41:41.840
you have the username, the
time this compromise happened,

00:41:41.840 --> 00:41:43.013
and the alert type.

00:41:43.013 --> 00:41:44.930
And this is something
that you definitely want

00:41:44.930 --> 00:41:47.550
to go ahead and investigate.

00:41:47.550 --> 00:41:50.780
So this brings us to the Alert
Center investigations dashboard

00:41:50.780 --> 00:41:54.500
in Sumo Logic, where we've
automatically correlated Alert

00:41:54.500 --> 00:41:56.990
Center data with all
of G Suite activity,

00:41:56.990 --> 00:42:00.020
and we have these two panels
that show all the G Suite

00:42:00.020 --> 00:42:02.970
activities by compromised users.

00:42:02.970 --> 00:42:06.150
Similarly, you also want
to look into all the logins

00:42:06.150 --> 00:42:10.260
by compromised users to
determine how active they are

00:42:10.260 --> 00:42:12.810
and where they're coming from.

00:42:12.810 --> 00:42:15.030
This kind of ability,
where we focus

00:42:15.030 --> 00:42:19.390
our panels on all activities and
logins by compromised users--

00:42:19.390 --> 00:42:21.840
we also have panels for
compromised devices--

00:42:21.840 --> 00:42:25.170
we've seen helps security
analysts and security

00:42:25.170 --> 00:42:29.040
teams cut down the amount of
time required to investigate

00:42:29.040 --> 00:42:31.740
an alert or incident.

00:42:31.740 --> 00:42:34.200
So we've talked about
correlating Alert Center

00:42:34.200 --> 00:42:37.470
data with G Suite activity, but
what about your other business

00:42:37.470 --> 00:42:39.060
applications?

00:42:39.060 --> 00:42:41.130
So here, we are
seeing an example

00:42:41.130 --> 00:42:44.760
on the right where we are
doing a search in Sumo Logic

00:42:44.760 --> 00:42:48.120
across all of
Salesforce.com event data

00:42:48.120 --> 00:42:51.900
to get a list of all the reports
downloaded by a compromised

00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:55.230
user that was detected
by Alert Center.

00:42:55.230 --> 00:42:58.980
So having this capability
of investigating data

00:42:58.980 --> 00:43:02.280
across various
applications is something

00:43:02.280 --> 00:43:05.520
that is super valuable
for our customers,

00:43:05.520 --> 00:43:10.830
and that's why they use us
for their security use cases.

00:43:10.830 --> 00:43:12.780
I also wanted to point
out that you can easily

00:43:12.780 --> 00:43:16.110
create your own
dashboards in Sumo Logic

00:43:16.110 --> 00:43:19.410
by combining dashboard
panels from various apps,

00:43:19.410 --> 00:43:21.970
or even creating
some of your own.

00:43:21.970 --> 00:43:24.480
So by doing this, you can
create a dashboard that's

00:43:24.480 --> 00:43:27.630
very specific to your
company or organization,

00:43:27.630 --> 00:43:32.020
and you get a quick overview
of all the security aspects,

00:43:32.020 --> 00:43:35.550
whether it's endpoints,
network identity management

00:43:35.550 --> 00:43:42.060
systems, cloud platforms, or
even on-premise data sources.

00:43:42.060 --> 00:43:44.990
So now that we've looked
into how to monitor, detect,

00:43:44.990 --> 00:43:48.620
and investigate
security alerts, let's

00:43:48.620 --> 00:43:51.200
talk about how to
automatically remediate these

00:43:51.200 --> 00:43:53.750
when they happen again.

00:43:53.750 --> 00:43:57.920
So this is a document
from the G Suite Help

00:43:57.920 --> 00:44:02.720
that talks about how to identify
and secure compromised G Suite

00:44:02.720 --> 00:44:04.230
accounts.

00:44:04.230 --> 00:44:06.395
So this is a four-step
process, and this

00:44:06.395 --> 00:44:07.610
is an example of a workflow.

00:44:11.120 --> 00:44:12.890
Creating and managing
these workflows

00:44:12.890 --> 00:44:16.130
in a consistent manner is
critical for maintaining

00:44:16.130 --> 00:44:19.020
your overall security posture.

00:44:19.020 --> 00:44:22.260
What we, at Sumo Logic,
do is help automate

00:44:22.260 --> 00:44:24.270
the creation of these
incident response

00:44:24.270 --> 00:44:27.720
workflows by sending data
to a number of ticketing

00:44:27.720 --> 00:44:31.020
notification and
response systems.

00:44:31.020 --> 00:44:35.670
We also see that this
kind of workflow creation,

00:44:35.670 --> 00:44:39.990
and sending critical
data about what happened,

00:44:39.990 --> 00:44:41.970
helps in reducing the
time to investigate

00:44:41.970 --> 00:44:45.120
by providing context around
an alert or incident.

00:44:45.120 --> 00:44:48.450
So for example, listing
out all the activities

00:44:48.450 --> 00:44:51.480
that happened by a
particular compromised user.

00:44:51.480 --> 00:44:53.490
Finally, creating
these workflows

00:44:53.490 --> 00:44:54.900
is also something
that we've seen

00:44:54.900 --> 00:44:58.800
that helps prevent alert
fatigue by sending data

00:44:58.800 --> 00:45:01.350
to the right teams that
have specific areas

00:45:01.350 --> 00:45:03.390
of responsibility,
as opposed to sending

00:45:03.390 --> 00:45:07.310
all alerts to the
entire security team.

00:45:07.310 --> 00:45:10.430
So just to summarize our
experience as a partner,

00:45:10.430 --> 00:45:13.690
we've seen how G Suite and
Alert Center have given us

00:45:13.690 --> 00:45:17.050
critical data to further
enable our customers

00:45:17.050 --> 00:45:20.980
to monitor, detect, investigate,
and respond to security alerts

00:45:20.980 --> 00:45:22.360
and threats.

